# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-avc/openavc-drivers/main/avcdriver.schema.json
#
# Sennheiser TeamConnect Ceiling 2 (TCC2) beamforming ceiling microphone
#
# Controls the TeamConnect Ceiling 2 over Sennheiser Sound Control (SSC), the
# JSON-over-UDP media control protocol on port 45.
#
# Protocol reference: Sennheiser Sound Control Protocol (SSC) — Media control
# protocol, TeamConnect Ceiling 2, Firmware Version 1.8.0 (TI 1245 v1.8.0).
# Archived: driver-roadmap/reference-docs/sennheiser-ssc-tcc2-v1.8.0.pdf
#
# Wire format (spec §4):
#   Every message is one JSON object, one object per UDP datagram. The object
#   is an address tree: {"audio":{"mute":true}} sets /audio/mute, and a null
#   argument is a query: {"audio":{"mute":null}} reads it. The reply carries
#   the resulting value in the same tree, so a setter's answer IS the readback
#   (an out-of-range number comes back adapted, not refused). Several methods
#   may share one message. Faults arrive as {"osc":{"error":[ ...tree... ]}}
#   with a three-digit code and a "desc" (spec §5.1.2).
#
# Transport (spec §6): UDP is the transport every SSC device MUST implement
# and the one the TeamConnect Ceiling 2 document lists first; TCP on the same
# port is OPTIONAL in the spec and nothing in Sennheiser's TCC2 documents says
# the microphone offers it, so this driver speaks UDP. An SSC session over UDP
# lasts 60 s past the last successful method call (spec §4.3.3), which is why
# the liveness probe below pings every 20 s: it proves the microphone is there
# AND keeps the session, and with it every subscription, alive.
#
# Push, not polling (spec §5.1.9): the microphone notifies a subscribed client
# on every value change, on the same socket the request came from, so there is
# no push: block (that primitive is for channels the platform must open).
# on_connect subscribes to the whole control surface; the subscription reply
# is bundled with the current values, so the device is fully populated before
# the first poll. The poll cycle re-sends the same subscriptions: a renewal is
# indistinguishable from a first request, so a session the microphone dropped
# (reboot, a >60 s gap) re-arms itself within one poll interval, and the
# renewal reply doubles as a full resync.
#
# Talker position and level meters are opt-in. /m/beam/azimuth and
# /m/beam/elevation follow the active talker; /m/in1/peak and /m/ref1/rms are
# live meters. Each is a continuous feed once subscribed, so both stay behind a
# config switch, are rate-limited on the microphone itself ("#":{"max":..} in
# the subscription, the spec's "notifications are sent not earlier than this
# many ms apart" parameter), throttled again in the response rules, and relay
# to the cloud at low priority. Both can also be switched at runtime from a
# macro or panel button.
#
# Exclusion zones, the priority zone and the equalizer are array-valued
# methods. SSC accepts null for "leave this element alone" (spec §4.3.1
# "Combined query-and-change", and the exclusion-zone examples in §7.47), so
# every one of those values is a device setting that writes its own slot and
# nulls the rest. Zone on/off is also a command whose zone picker carries the
# positional row.
#
# Format: YAML. Every method is a fixed JSON string, every reply parses with
# json: true rules, and the subscription is a query like any other; nothing
# here needs code.
#
# NOT hardware-verified. Built from the specification and its own examples;
# the quirks worth checking on a microphone are listed in the shipped record
# (driver-roadmap/shipped/sennheiser_tcc2.md).

id: sennheiser_tcc2
name: Sennheiser TeamConnect Ceiling 2
manufacturer: Sennheiser
category: audio
version: "1.1.0"
author: OpenAVC
min_platform_version: "0.34.0"
description: >
  Controls the Sennheiser TeamConnect Ceiling 2 beamforming ceiling microphone
  over Sennheiser Sound Control (JSON over UDP, port 45). Mute, room activity,
  analog and Dante output levels, AEC reference gain, the 7-band equalizer,
  noise gate, Voice Lift, priority and exclusion zones, installation type,
  the LED ring colours and brightness, device naming, identify, restart and
  restore. The microphone reports where the active talker is (beam azimuth and
  elevation) and live input and reference meters; both feeds are opt-in and
  can be switched from a macro or panel. State is push-driven: the driver
  subscribes and the microphone reports every change as it happens, including
  changes made from Sennheiser Control Cockpit.

source_url: https://www.sennheiser.com/globalassets/digizuite/41940-en-ti_1245_v1.8.0_sennheiser_sound_control_protocol_tcc2_en.pdf
tags: [microphone, ceiling-mic, beamforming, array, conferencing, dante, camera-tracking, ssc]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [ssc]
ports: [45]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Sennheiser
    models: [TeamConnect Ceiling 2]
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Built from Sennheiser's SSC developer guide for firmware 1.8.0; not yet
      run against a microphone. Every method in that guide is covered except
      the network address configuration and firmware update, which belong to
      Sennheiser Control Cockpit.

transport: udp

help:
  overview: >
    Controls the Sennheiser TeamConnect Ceiling 2, a ceiling microphone that
    steers one pickup beam at whoever is talking. Mute it, set its output
    levels and processing, change the LED ring, and read where the talker is
    (azimuth and elevation) to drive camera presets from a macro. Everything
    the microphone changes, from Control Cockpit or its own button, shows up
    here as it happens.
  setup: >
    1. Set the microphone up once in Sennheiser Control Cockpit (it must be
       configured there before any control system can talk to it) and note
       its IP address.
    2. Enter that address here. Control uses UDP port 45; leave the port
       alone unless Sennheiser support changed it.
    3. Talker Position and Level Meters are off by default. Each one makes
       the microphone stream continuously, so turn one on only when you bind
       it, and raise its interval if you want less traffic. The settings here
       decide what happens on connect; the Talker Position On/Off and Level
       Meters On/Off commands switch them while running, so a panel can start
       the feed when a page opens and stop it when the page closes.
    4. Exclusion zones (where the beam must never point) and the priority
       zone live in this device's settings, one value per angle, and follow
       the same 5 degree steps as Control Cockpit. Zone on/off is also a
       command for macros.
    5. The microphone and the OpenAVC server must be able to exchange UDP
       traffic on port 45 in both directions. If the microphone shows offline
       while Control Cockpit still sees it, check for a firewall between the
       two.
  connection: >
    The microphone answers UDP port 45 only after its first configuration in
    Sennheiser Control Cockpit. If Control Cockpit sees it and OpenAVC does
    not, a firewall between the server and the microphone is blocking UDP 45.

discovery:
  # One SSC message asks two things: the installation type, whose two possible
  # answers only a TeamConnect Ceiling 2 gives (other Sennheiser SSC devices
  # answer that address with a 404), and the product string for the model
  # column. Every SSC device answers UDP 45, so the port alone proves nothing.
  # The probe is sent to each subnet's broadcast address; whether a
  # microphone answers a broadcast datagram (the spec says an SSC server MUST
  # respond to every message it receives) is one of the things to confirm on
  # hardware.
  udp_probe:
    port: 45
    send_ascii: '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null}},"audio":{"installation_type":null}}'
    expect_regex: '"installation_type":"(?:flush_mount|suspended)"'
    timeout_ms: 1500
    extract:
      model:
        regex: '"product":"([^"]+)"'
        group: 1
    extract_manufacturer: "Sennheiser"
  oui:
    - "00:1b:66"   # Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "sennheiser"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 45
  poll_interval: 30
  inter_command_delay: 0.05
  enable_talker_position: false
  talker_interval_ms: 500
  enable_level_meters: false
  meter_interval_ms: 500

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: IP Address
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 45
    label: UDP Port
    help: "Sennheiser Sound Control listens on UDP port 45."
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 0
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
    help: >
      How often the subscriptions are renewed, which also re-reads every
      value. The microphone pushes changes between polls, so 30 s is plenty.
  inter_command_delay:
    type: number
    default: 0.05
    label: Inter-Command Delay (sec)
  enable_talker_position:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Enable Talker Position
    help: >
      Report the direction of the active talker (Beam Azimuth and Beam
      Elevation) for driving camera presets from macros. The microphone
      streams this continuously once enabled, so leave it off unless you use
      it.
  talker_interval_ms:
    type: integer
    default: 500
    min: 50
    max: 60000
    label: Talker Position Interval (ms)
    help: >
      Shortest gap between talker position updates. Applied on connect while
      Enable Talker Position is on, and by the Talker Position On command.
  enable_level_meters:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Enable Level Meters
    help: >
      Stream the microphone's input peak level and the AEC reference level
      into OpenAVC. Continuous once enabled, so leave it off unless you bind
      a meter on a panel.
  meter_interval_ms:
    type: integer
    default: 500
    min: 50
    max: 60000
    label: Meter Interval (ms)
    help: >
      Shortest gap between meter updates. Applied on connect while Enable
      Level Meters is on, and by the Level Meters On command.

# UDP has no connection to drop, so the microphone's own ping is the liveness
# signal: two silent probes force a reconnect with a typed no_response fault.
# 20 s also keeps the SSC session (and every subscription) alive, which the
# spec ends 60 s after the last successful call.
liveness:
  send: '{"osc":{"ping":null}}'
  expect: '"ping"'
  interval: 20
  timeout: 5
  max_failures: 2

# Constants are read once; everything that can change is subscribed. The
# subscription reply is bundled with the current values, so this is also the
# initial sync. Split into a few datagrams so none approaches a UDP MTU.
on_connect:
  - '{"device":{"identity":{"product":null,"version":null,"serial":null,"vendor":null,"hw_revision":null},"language":null,"network":{"ether":{"macs":null}}},"interface":{"version":null},"audio":{"out1":{"label":null},"out2":{"label":null,"identity":{"version":null}},"ref1":{"label":null}}}'
  - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"audio":{"mute":null,"room_in_use":null,"installation_type":null,"out1":{"attenuation":null},"out2":{"gain":null,"network":{"ether":{"interface_mapping":null},"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}},"ref1":{"gain":null,"farend_auto_adjust_enable":null},"source_detection":{"threshold":null}}}]}}}'
  - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":null,"custom":null},"noise_gate":{"active":null,"threshold":null,"hold_time":null},"voice_lift":{"active":null,"emergency_mute_threshold":null,"emergency_mute_time":null},"priority":{"zones":null,"weights":null,"active":null},"exclusion":{"zones":null,"active":null}}}]}}}'
  - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"device":{"name":null,"location":null,"position":null,"system":null,"identification":{"visual":null},"button":{"state":null},"update":{"progress":null,"error":null,"enable":null},"led":{"brightness":null,"mic_on":{"color":null},"mic_mute":{"color":null},"custom":{"color":null,"active":null},"show_farend_activity":null},"network":{"mdns":null,"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}},"beam":{"orientation":{"offset":null,"visual":null}}}]}}}'
  - send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{talker_interval_ms}},"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":null,"elevation":null}}}]}}}'
    when: enable_talker_position
  - send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{meter_interval_ms}},"m":{"in1":{"peak":null},"ref1":{"rms":null}}}]}}}'
    when: enable_level_meters

# Renew every subscription each cycle: a renewal is the same message as the
# first request (spec §5.1.9), it re-arms a session the microphone dropped,
# and its reply carries every current value, so one cycle is a full resync.
polling:
  queries:
    - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"audio":{"mute":null,"room_in_use":null,"installation_type":null,"out1":{"attenuation":null},"out2":{"gain":null,"network":{"ether":{"interface_mapping":null},"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}},"ref1":{"gain":null,"farend_auto_adjust_enable":null},"source_detection":{"threshold":null}}}]}}}'
    - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":null,"custom":null},"noise_gate":{"active":null,"threshold":null,"hold_time":null},"voice_lift":{"active":null,"emergency_mute_threshold":null,"emergency_mute_time":null},"priority":{"zones":null,"weights":null,"active":null},"exclusion":{"zones":null,"active":null}}}]}}}'
    - '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"device":{"name":null,"location":null,"position":null,"system":null,"identification":{"visual":null},"button":{"state":null},"update":{"progress":null,"error":null,"enable":null},"led":{"brightness":null,"mic_on":{"color":null},"mic_mute":{"color":null},"custom":{"color":null,"active":null},"show_farend_activity":null},"network":{"mdns":null,"ipv4":{"ipaddr":null}}},"beam":{"orientation":{"offset":null,"visual":null}}}]}}}'
    - send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{talker_interval_ms}},"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":null,"elevation":null}}}]}}}'
      when: enable_talker_position
    - send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{meter_interval_ms}},"m":{"in1":{"peak":null},"ref1":{"rms":null}}}]}}}'
      when: enable_level_meters

state_variables:
  # ── Identity ──
  product:
    type: string
    label: Product
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Version
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
  vendor:
    type: string
    label: Vendor
  hardware_revision:
    type: string
    label: Hardware Revision
  interface_version:
    type: string
    label: SSC Interface Version
    help: "Version of the microphone's control address tree."
  language:
    type: string
    label: Language
  mac_address:
    type: string
    label: MAC Address
  ip_address:
    type: string
    label: IP Address (on device)
    help: "Control-port address the microphone reports for itself."
  mdns_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: mDNS Advertising
    help: "True when the microphone announces itself on the network (Bonjour)."
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "Name set on the microphone (up to 8 characters)."
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
    help: "Room and building, as set on the microphone."
  position:
    type: string
    label: Position in Room
    help: "Where in the room this microphone sits, as set on the microphone."
  system_label:
    type: string
    label: System Label
    help: "Free-text system information stored on the microphone."

  # ── Live state ──
  mute:
    type: boolean
    label: Muted
    control: true
    cloud_priority: high
    help: "True when the microphone is muted. Mutes every output."
  room_in_use:
    type: boolean
    label: Room In Use
    cloud_priority: high
    help: >
      True while the microphone hears someone talking. Bind a trigger to it
      for occupancy-driven automation.
  identify_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Identify Active
    help: "True while the LED ring is blinking to identify the microphone (10 s)."
  reset_button_pressed:
    type: boolean
    label: Reset Button Pressed
  beam_azimuth:
    type: integer
    label: Beam Azimuth
    min: 0
    max: 359
    unit: deg
    cloud_priority: low
    help: >
      Direction of the active talker, 0 to 359 degrees from the microphone's
      0 degree reference (Beam Orientation Offset). Updates only while Talker
      Position is on; holds the last direction when the room is quiet.
  beam_elevation:
    type: integer
    label: Beam Elevation
    min: 0
    max: 90
    unit: deg
    cloud_priority: low
    help: >
      Elevation of the active talker, 0 (horizon) to 90 (straight down).
      Updates only while Talker Position is on.
  input_peak_db:
    type: number
    label: Input Peak Level
    min: -90
    max: 0
    unit: dB
    cloud_priority: low
    help: "Microphone input peak. Updates only while Level Meters is on."
  reference_rms_db:
    type: number
    label: AEC Reference Level
    min: -120
    max: 0
    unit: dBFS
    cloud_priority: low
    help: >
      RMS level of the far-end (AEC reference) signal arriving over Dante.
      Updates only while Level Meters is on.

  # ── Outputs and reference ──
  out1_label:
    type: string
    label: Analog Output Label
  output_attenuation:
    type: number
    label: Analog Output Attenuation
    min: -18
    max: 0
    step: 1
    unit: dB
    control: true
    help: "Attenuation applied to the analog (Phoenix) output, -18 to 0 dB."
  out2_label:
    type: string
    label: Dante Output Label
  dante_output_gain:
    type: number
    label: Dante Output Gain
    min: 0
    max: 24
    step: 1
    unit: dB
    control: true
    help: "Gain applied to the Dante output, 0 to +24 dB."
  dante_firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: Dante Firmware Version
  dante_ip_primary:
    type: string
    label: Dante Primary IP
  dante_ip_secondary:
    type: string
    label: Dante Secondary IP
  dante_interface_mapping:
    type: enum
    values: [AUDIO_SWITCHED, AUDIO_REDUNDANT]
    label: Dante Port Mode
    help: "Switched (one network on both ports) or Redundant (primary and secondary)."
  ref1_label:
    type: string
    label: AEC Reference Label
  reference_gain:
    type: number
    label: AEC Reference Gain
    min: -60
    max: 10
    step: 1
    unit: dB
    control: true
    help: "Gain applied to the far-end signal the echo canceller listens to."
  farend_auto_adjust:
    type: boolean
    label: Far-End Auto Adjust
    help: "True when the AEC threshold follows the estimated noise floor."

  # ── Processing ──
  installation_type:
    type: enum
    values: [flush_mount, suspended]
    label: Installation Type
    help: "Flush against the ceiling, or suspended at least 30 cm below it."
  source_detection_threshold:
    type: enum
    values: [quiet_room, normal_room, loud_room]
    label: Source Detection Threshold
    help: "How loud a talker must be, relative to the room, to steer the beam."
  eq_preset:
    type: enum
    values: ["OFF", CUSTOM]
    label: Equalizer
    help: "OFF bypasses the equalizer; CUSTOM applies the seven band gains."
  eq_125_hz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 125 Hz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_250_hz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 250 Hz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_500_hz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 500 Hz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_1_khz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 1 kHz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_2_khz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 2 kHz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_4_khz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 4 kHz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  eq_8_khz:
    type: number
    label: EQ 8 kHz
    min: -8
    max: 8
    step: 0.5
    unit: dB
  noise_gate_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Noise Gate
  noise_gate_threshold:
    type: number
    label: Noise Gate Threshold
    min: -90
    max: -40
    step: 1
    unit: dB
    help: "Level that opens the gate. A built-in hysteresis closes it again."
  noise_gate_hold_time:
    type: integer
    label: Noise Gate Hold Time
    min: 50
    max: 1000
    step: 10
    unit: ms
    help: "Shortest time the gate stays open once triggered."
  voice_lift_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Voice Lift
    help: "True when the feedback-reduction processing for voice lift is on."
  voice_lift_mute_threshold:
    type: number
    label: Voice Lift Emergency Mute Threshold
    min: -50
    max: -3
    step: 1
    unit: dB
    help: "Microphone level above which Voice Lift mutes the output briefly."
  voice_lift_mute_time:
    type: number
    label: Voice Lift Emergency Mute Time
    min: 1
    max: 30
    step: 1
    unit: s
    help: "How long the emergency mute lasts."

  # ── Priority zone (one zone: the talkers the beam should favour) ──
  priority_zone_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Priority Zone
  priority_zone_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  priority_zone_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  priority_zone_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  priority_zone_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Priority Zone Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  priority_zone_weight:
    type: number
    label: Priority Zone Weight
    min: 1
    max: 4
    step: 0.1
    help: "How strongly the beam favours the priority zone (1.0 = neutral)."

  # ── Exclusion zones (five: where the beam must never point) ──
  exclusion_zone_1_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 1
  exclusion_zone_1_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_1_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_2_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 2
  exclusion_zone_2_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_2_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_3_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 3
  exclusion_zone_3_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_3_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_4_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 4
  exclusion_zone_4_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_4_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_5_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Exclusion Zone 5
  exclusion_zone_5_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Elevation Min
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_5_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Elevation Max
    min: 0
    max: 90
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Azimuth Min
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg
  exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Azimuth Max
    min: 0
    max: 360
    step: 5
    unit: deg

  # ── Orientation ──
  beam_orientation_offset:
    type: integer
    label: Beam Orientation Offset
    min: 0
    max: 270
    step: 90
    unit: deg
    help: >
      Rotates the 0 degree reference of every azimuth value to match how the
      microphone is mounted (0, 90, 180 or 270).
  orientation_leds_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Orientation LEDs
    help: "True while two LEDs show the microphone's 0 degree direction."

  # ── LED ring ──
  led_brightness:
    type: integer
    label: LED Brightness
    min: 0
    max: 5
    step: 1
    control: true
    help: "0 turns the LED ring off; 5 is brightest."
  mic_on_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Mic On Colour
    help: "LED ring colour while the microphone is live."
  mic_mute_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Mic Mute Colour
    help: "LED ring colour while the microphone is muted."
  custom_led_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Custom LED Colour
    help: "Colour shown while Custom LED is active."
  custom_led_active:
    type: boolean
    label: Custom LED Active
    help: >
      True while the ring shows the custom colour instead of the mic on/mute
      colours. Resets to off when the microphone reboots.
  show_farend_activity:
    type: boolean
    label: Far-End Activity LED
    help: "True when the ring also indicates audio arriving from the far end."

  # ── Firmware update, as reported by the microphone ──
  update_running:
    type: boolean
    label: Firmware Update Running
  update_progress:
    type: integer
    label: Firmware Update Progress
    min: 0
    max: 100
    unit: "%"
  update_error:
    type: string
    label: Firmware Update Result

  # ── Last protocol error ──
  last_error_code:
    type: integer
    label: Last Error Code
    help: "SSC error code of the last refused request (404 unknown address, 406 bad value)."
  last_error:
    type: string
    label: Last Error
    help: "The microphone's description of the last refused request."

commands:
  # ── Mute ──
  mute_on:
    label: Mute On
    send: '{"audio":{"mute":true}}'
    help: "Mute the microphone (every output)."
  mute_off:
    label: Mute Off
    send: '{"audio":{"mute":false}}'

  # ── Levels ──
  set_output_attenuation:
    label: Set Analog Output Attenuation
    send: '{"audio":{"out1":{"attenuation":{level}}}}'
    help: "Attenuate the analog output, -18 to 0 dB."
    params:
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Attenuation
        min: -18
        max: 0
        unit: dB
  set_dante_gain:
    label: Set Dante Output Gain
    send: '{"audio":{"out2":{"gain":{gain}}}}'
    params:
      gain:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Gain
        min: 0
        max: 24
        unit: dB
  set_reference_gain:
    label: Set AEC Reference Gain
    send: '{"audio":{"ref1":{"gain":{gain}}}}'
    help: "Gain applied to the far-end signal the echo canceller listens to."
    params:
      gain:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Gain
        min: -60
        max: 10
        unit: dB

  # ── Equalizer ──
  eq_on:
    label: Equalizer On
    send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":"CUSTOM"}}}'
    help: "Apply the seven band gains."
  eq_off:
    label: Equalizer Off
    send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":"OFF"}}}'
    help: "Bypass the equalizer. The band gains are kept."
  set_eq:
    label: Set Equalizer Bands
    send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[{g125},{g250},{g500},{g1k},{g2k},{g4k},{g8k}]}}}'
    help: "Set all seven bands at once, -8 to +8 dB in 0.5 dB steps. Each band is also a device setting."
    params:
      g125: { type: number, required: true, label: 125 Hz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g250: { type: number, required: true, label: 250 Hz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g500: { type: number, required: true, label: 500 Hz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g1k: { type: number, required: true, label: 1 kHz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g2k: { type: number, required: true, label: 2 kHz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g4k: { type: number, required: true, label: 4 kHz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }
      g8k: { type: number, required: true, label: 8 kHz, min: -8, max: 8, unit: dB }

  # ── Noise gate and Voice Lift ──
  noise_gate_on:
    label: Noise Gate On
    send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"active":true}}}'
  noise_gate_off:
    label: Noise Gate Off
    send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"active":false}}}'
  set_noise_gate:
    label: Set Noise Gate
    send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"threshold":{threshold},"hold_time":{hold_time}}}}'
    params:
      threshold:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Threshold
        min: -90
        max: -40
        unit: dB
      hold_time:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Hold Time
        min: 50
        max: 1000
        unit: ms
  voice_lift_on:
    label: Voice Lift On
    send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"active":true}}}'
    help: "Turn on the feedback-reduction processing for rooms that reinforce the microphone through loudspeakers."
  voice_lift_off:
    label: Voice Lift Off
    send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"active":false}}}'
  set_voice_lift_emergency_mute:
    label: Set Voice Lift Emergency Mute
    send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"emergency_mute_threshold":{threshold},"emergency_mute_time":{time}}}}'
    help: "Level above which Voice Lift mutes the output, and for how long."
    params:
      threshold:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Threshold
        min: -50
        max: -3
        unit: dB
      time:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: Mute Time
        min: 1
        max: 30
        unit: s

  # ── Pickup ──
  set_source_detection:
    label: Set Source Detection Threshold
    send: '{"audio":{"source_detection":{"threshold":"{threshold}"}}}'
    help: "How loud a talker must be, relative to the room, to steer the beam."
    params:
      threshold:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Room
        values:
          - { value: quiet_room, label: Quiet room }
          - { value: normal_room, label: Normal room }
          - { value: loud_room, label: Loud room }
  set_installation_type:
    label: Set Installation Type
    send: '{"audio":{"installation_type":"{type}"}}'
    params:
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Installation
        values:
          - { value: flush_mount, label: Flush mount }
          - { value: suspended, label: Suspended }

  # ── Zones ──
  # A zone's on/off flag lives in a five-element array; the zone picker carries
  # the whole positional row, null meaning "leave that zone as it is".
  exclusion_zone_on:
    label: Exclusion Zone On
    send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[{zone}]}}}'
    help: "Activate one of the five exclusion zones. Its angles are in this device's settings."
    params:
      zone:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Zone
        values: ["1", "2", "3", "4", "5"]
        map:
          "1": "true,null,null,null,null"
          "2": "null,true,null,null,null"
          "3": "null,null,true,null,null"
          "4": "null,null,null,true,null"
          "5": "null,null,null,null,true"
  exclusion_zone_off:
    label: Exclusion Zone Off
    send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[{zone}]}}}'
    params:
      zone:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Zone
        values: ["1", "2", "3", "4", "5"]
        map:
          "1": "false,null,null,null,null"
          "2": "null,false,null,null,null"
          "3": "null,null,false,null,null"
          "4": "null,null,null,false,null"
          "5": "null,null,null,null,false"
  priority_zone_on:
    label: Priority Zone On
    send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"active":[true]}}}'
    help: "Make the beam favour talkers inside the priority zone."
  priority_zone_off:
    label: Priority Zone Off
    send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"active":[false]}}}'
  set_priority_zone:
    label: Set Priority Zone
    send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"zones":[{elevation_min},{elevation_max},{azimuth_min},{azimuth_max}]}}}'
    help: "Angles of the priority zone, in 5 degree steps; each angle is also a device setting."
    params:
      elevation_min: { type: integer, required: true, label: Elevation Min, min: 0, max: 90, unit: deg }
      elevation_max: { type: integer, required: true, label: Elevation Max, min: 0, max: 90, unit: deg }
      azimuth_min: { type: integer, required: true, label: Azimuth Min, min: 0, max: 360, unit: deg }
      azimuth_max: { type: integer, required: true, label: Azimuth Max, min: 0, max: 360, unit: deg }

  # ── LED ring ──
  set_led_brightness:
    label: Set LED Brightness
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"brightness":{level}}}}'
    help: "0 turns the ring off; 5 is brightest."
    params:
      level:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: Brightness
        min: 0
        max: 5
  set_mic_on_color:
    label: Set Mic On Colour
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_on":{"color":"{color}"}}}}'
    params:
      color:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Colour
        values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
  set_mic_mute_color:
    label: Set Mic Mute Colour
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_mute":{"color":"{color}"}}}}'
    params:
      color:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Colour
        values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
  custom_led_on:
    label: Custom LED Colour On
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"color":"{color}","active":true}}}}'
    help: "Show a colour of your choice on the ring instead of the mic on/mute colours, until Custom LED Colour Off or a reboot."
    params:
      color:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Colour
        values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
  custom_led_off:
    label: Custom LED Colour Off
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"active":false}}}}'
  farend_activity_led_on:
    label: Far-End Activity LED On
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"show_farend_activity":true}}}'
    help: "Let the ring also show audio arriving from the far end."
  farend_activity_led_off:
    label: Far-End Activity LED Off
    send: '{"device":{"led":{"show_farend_activity":false}}}'
  identify:
    label: Identify
    send: '{"device":{"identification":{"visual":true}}}'
    help: "Blink the LED ring for 10 seconds so you can find this microphone in the ceiling."

  # ── Orientation ──
  set_orientation_offset:
    label: Set Beam Orientation Offset
    send: '{"beam":{"orientation":{"offset":{offset}}}}'
    help: "Rotate the 0 degree reference to match the mounting: 0, 90, 180 or 270 degrees."
    params:
      offset:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Offset
        values: ["0", "90", "180", "270"]
  orientation_leds_on:
    label: Orientation LEDs On
    send: '{"beam":{"orientation":{"visual":true}}}'
    help: "Light two LEDs showing the microphone's 0 degree direction (green right, red left)."
  orientation_leds_off:
    label: Orientation LEDs Off
    send: '{"beam":{"orientation":{"visual":false}}}'

  # ── Talker position and meters, switchable at runtime ──
  # The config switches decide what is armed on connect; these subscribe and
  # cancel the same feeds while running, so a panel pays for the stream only
  # while it is on screen.
  get_beam_position:
    label: Get Talker Position
    send: '{"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":null,"elevation":null}}}'
    help: >
      Read the talker's direction once and update Beam Azimuth and Beam
      Elevation. Use this instead of Talker Position On when a macro needs
      the direction at one moment rather than continuously.
  talker_position_on:
    label: Talker Position On
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{talker_interval_ms}},"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":null,"elevation":null}}}]}}}'
    help: "Start the talker position feed (Beam Azimuth and Beam Elevation). Continuous until Talker Position Off."
  talker_position_off:
    label: Talker Position Off
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"cancel":true},"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":null,"elevation":null}}}]}}}'
  meters_on:
    label: Level Meters On
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"max":{meter_interval_ms}},"m":{"in1":{"peak":null},"ref1":{"rms":null}}}]}}}'
    help: "Start the live meter feed (Input Peak Level and AEC Reference Level). Continuous until Level Meters Off."
  meters_off:
    label: Level Meters Off
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"#":{"cancel":true},"m":{"in1":{"peak":null},"ref1":{"rms":null}}}]}}}'

  # ── Device ──
  set_device_name:
    label: Set Device Name
    send: '{"device":{"name":"{name}"}}'
    help: "Up to 8 characters: letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter and ending with a letter or digit."
    params:
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: Name
        pattern: '^[A-Za-z](?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,6}[A-Za-z0-9])?$'
  restart:
    label: Restart
    send: '{"device":{"restart":true}}'
    help: "Reboot the microphone. Audio drops for about a minute."
  restore:
    label: Restore Defaults
    send: '{"device":{"restore":"{scope}"}}'
    help: >
      Audio Defaults resets the audio settings and keeps the microphone
      running. Factory Defaults and Dante Factory Defaults also reset the
      network settings and reboot, so the microphone may come back on a
      different address.
    params:
      scope:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: Restore
        values:
          - { value: AUDIO_DEFAULTS, label: "Audio defaults (no reboot)" }
          - { value: FACTORY_DEFAULTS, label: "Factory defaults (reboots, resets network)" }
          - { value: DANTE_FACTORY_DEFAULTS, label: "Dante factory defaults (reboots)" }
  refresh:
    label: Refresh From Device
    send: '{"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[{"audio":{"mute":null,"room_in_use":null,"installation_type":null,"out1":{"attenuation":null},"out2":{"gain":null}},"device":{"name":null,"led":{"brightness":null}}}]}}}'
    help: "Re-read the microphone's main values now. The poll does this automatically."

device_settings:
  # ── Naming ──
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: Device Name
    help: "Up to 8 characters: letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter and ending with a letter or digit."
    state_key: device_name
    default: "SLCM2"
    regex: '^[A-Za-z](?:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,6}[A-Za-z0-9])?$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
  location:
    type: string
    label: Location
    help: "Room and building, up to 100 characters."
    state_key: location
    default: "Room"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
  position:
    type: string
    label: Position in Room
    help: "Where in the room this microphone sits, up to 30 characters (letters, digits and spaces)."
    state_key: position
    default: "over central table"
    regex: '^[A-Za-z0-9 ]{0,30}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"position":"{value}"}}'
  system_label:
    type: string
    label: System Label
    help: "Free text stored on the microphone, up to 30 characters."
    state_key: system_label
    default: "System"
    regex: '^.{0,30}$'
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"system":"{value}"}}'

  # ── Pickup ──
  installation_type:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: flush_mount, label: Flush mount }
      - { value: suspended, label: Suspended (30 cm or more below the ceiling) }
    label: Installation Type
    help: "The microphone tunes its pickup for how it is mounted."
    state_key: installation_type
    default: flush_mount
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"installation_type":"{value}"}}'
  source_detection_threshold:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: quiet_room, label: Quiet room }
      - { value: normal_room, label: Normal room }
      - { value: loud_room, label: Loud room }
    label: Source Detection Threshold
    help: "How loud a talker must be, relative to the room, before the beam steers to them."
    state_key: source_detection_threshold
    default: normal_room
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"source_detection":{"threshold":"{value}"}}}'

  # ── Levels ──
  output_attenuation:
    type: number
    min: -18
    max: 0
    label: Analog Output Attenuation (dB)
    state_key: output_attenuation
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"out1":{"attenuation":{value}}}}'
  dante_output_gain:
    type: number
    min: 0
    max: 24
    label: Dante Output Gain (dB)
    state_key: dante_output_gain
    default: 12
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"out2":{"gain":{value}}}}'
  reference_gain:
    type: number
    min: -60
    max: 10
    label: AEC Reference Gain (dB)
    help: "Gain applied to the far-end signal the echo canceller listens to."
    state_key: reference_gain
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"ref1":{"gain":{value}}}}'
  farend_auto_adjust:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Far-End Auto Adjust
    help: "Let the AEC threshold follow the estimated noise floor."
    state_key: farend_auto_adjust
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"ref1":{"farend_auto_adjust_enable":{value}}}}'

  # ── Equalizer: seven bands at Q 1.41, each writes only its own slot ──
  eq_preset:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "OFF", label: "Off (bypass)" }
      - { value: CUSTOM, label: "On (custom bands)" }
    label: Equalizer
    state_key: eq_preset
    default: "OFF"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":"{value}"}}}'
  eq_125_hz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 125 Hz (dB)
    state_key: eq_125_hz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[{value},null,null,null,null,null,null]}}}'
  eq_250_hz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 250 Hz (dB)
    state_key: eq_250_hz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,{value},null,null,null,null,null]}}}'
  eq_500_hz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 500 Hz (dB)
    state_key: eq_500_hz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,null,{value},null,null,null,null]}}}'
  eq_1_khz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 1 kHz (dB)
    state_key: eq_1_khz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,null,null,{value},null,null,null]}}}'
  eq_2_khz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 2 kHz (dB)
    state_key: eq_2_khz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,null,null,null,{value},null,null]}}}'
  eq_4_khz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 4 kHz (dB)
    state_key: eq_4_khz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,null,null,null,null,{value},null]}}}'
  eq_8_khz:
    type: number
    min: -8
    max: 8
    label: EQ 8 kHz (dB)
    state_key: eq_8_khz
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"custom":[null,null,null,null,null,null,{value}]}}}'

  # ── Noise gate ──
  noise_gate_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Noise Gate
    state_key: noise_gate_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"active":{value}}}}'
  noise_gate_threshold:
    type: number
    min: -90
    max: -40
    label: Noise Gate Threshold (dB)
    help: "Level that opens the gate."
    state_key: noise_gate_threshold
    default: -60
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"threshold":{value}}}}'
  noise_gate_hold_time:
    type: integer
    min: 50
    max: 1000
    label: Noise Gate Hold Time (ms)
    state_key: noise_gate_hold_time
    default: 200
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"hold_time":{value}}}}'

  # ── Voice Lift ──
  voice_lift_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Voice Lift
    help: "Feedback reduction for rooms that reinforce the microphone through loudspeakers."
    state_key: voice_lift_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"active":{value}}}}'
  voice_lift_mute_threshold:
    type: number
    min: -50
    max: -3
    label: Voice Lift Emergency Mute Threshold (dB)
    help: "Microphone level above which Voice Lift mutes the output briefly."
    state_key: voice_lift_mute_threshold
    default: -20
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"emergency_mute_threshold":{value}}}}'
  voice_lift_mute_time:
    type: number
    min: 1
    max: 30
    label: Voice Lift Emergency Mute Time (s)
    state_key: voice_lift_mute_time
    default: 4
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"emergency_mute_time":{value}}}}'

  # ── Priority zone: [elevation min, elevation max, azimuth min, azimuth max] ──
  priority_zone_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Priority Zone
    help: "Make the beam favour talkers inside the zone below."
    state_key: priority_zone_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"active":[{value}]}}}'
  priority_zone_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Priority Zone Elevation Min (deg)
    help: "5 degree steps; the zone must span at least 10 degrees."
    state_key: priority_zone_elevation_min
    default: 60
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"zones":[{value},null,null,null]}}}'
  priority_zone_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Priority Zone Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: priority_zone_elevation_max
    default: 80
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"zones":[null,{value},null,null]}}}'
  priority_zone_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Priority Zone Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: priority_zone_azimuth_min
    default: 160
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"zones":[null,null,{value},null]}}}'
  priority_zone_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Priority Zone Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: priority_zone_azimuth_max
    default: 200
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"zones":[null,null,null,{value}]}}}'
  priority_zone_weight:
    type: number
    min: 1
    max: 4
    label: Priority Zone Weight
    help: "How strongly the beam favours the zone, 1.0 (neutral) to 4.0."
    state_key: priority_zone_weight
    default: 1.5
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"priority":{"weights":[{value}]}}}'

  # ── Exclusion zones: five rows of [elevation min, elevation max, azimuth min, azimuth max] ──
  # Each setting writes its own element and nulls the rest, so two settings
  # can change independently. Elevation 0 to 90, azimuth 0 to 360, 5 degree
  # steps, at least 10 degrees between min and max; equal azimuth min and max
  # means the full circle.
  exclusion_zone_1_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Exclusion Zone 1
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_active
    default: "true"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[{value},null,null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Elevation Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_elevation_min
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[[{value},null,null,null],null,null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_elevation_max
    default: 10
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[[null,{value},null,null],null,null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_min
    default: 0
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[[null,null,{value},null],null,null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 1 Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_max
    default: 360
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[[null,null,null,{value}],null,null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Exclusion Zone 2
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[null,{value},null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Elevation Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_elevation_min
    default: 10
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,[{value},null,null,null],null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_elevation_max
    default: 50
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,[null,{value},null,null],null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_min
    default: 20
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,[null,null,{value},null],null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 2 Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_max
    default: 70
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,[null,null,null,{value}],null,null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Exclusion Zone 3
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[null,null,{value},null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Elevation Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_elevation_min
    default: 10
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,[{value},null,null,null],null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_elevation_max
    default: 50
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,[null,{value},null,null],null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_min
    default: 110
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,[null,null,{value},null],null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 3 Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_max
    default: 160
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,[null,null,null,{value}],null,null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_4_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Exclusion Zone 4
    state_key: exclusion_zone_4_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[null,null,null,{value},null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_4_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Elevation Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_4_elevation_min
    default: 10
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,[{value},null,null,null],null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_4_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_4_elevation_max
    default: 50
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,[null,{value},null,null],null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_min
    default: 200
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,[null,null,{value},null],null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 4 Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_max
    default: 250
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,[null,null,null,{value}],null]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_5_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Exclusion Zone 5
    state_key: exclusion_zone_5_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"active":[null,null,null,null,{value}]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_5_elevation_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Elevation Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_5_elevation_min
    default: 10
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,null,[{value},null,null,null]]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_5_elevation_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 90
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Elevation Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_5_elevation_max
    default: 50
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,null,[null,{value},null,null]]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_min:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Azimuth Min (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_min
    default: 290
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,null,[null,null,{value},null]]}}}'
  exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_max:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 360
    label: Exclusion Zone 5 Azimuth Max (deg)
    state_key: exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_max
    default: 340
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"exclusion":{"zones":[null,null,null,null,[null,null,null,{value}]]}}}'

  # ── Orientation ──
  beam_orientation_offset:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "0", label: "0 degrees" }
      - { value: "90", label: "90 degrees" }
      - { value: "180", label: "180 degrees" }
      - { value: "270", label: "270 degrees" }
    label: Beam Orientation Offset
    help: "Rotate the 0 degree reference of every azimuth value to match how the microphone is mounted."
    state_key: beam_orientation_offset
    default: "0"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"beam":{"orientation":{"offset":{value}}}}'

  # ── LED ring ──
  led_brightness:
    type: integer
    min: 0
    max: 5
    label: LED Brightness
    help: "0 turns the ring off; 5 is brightest."
    state_key: led_brightness
    default: 5
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"brightness":{value}}}}'
  mic_on_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Mic On Colour
    help: "Ring colour while the microphone is live. Factory is GREEN."
    state_key: mic_on_color
    default: GREEN
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_on":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
  mic_mute_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Mic Mute Colour
    help: "Ring colour while the microphone is muted. Factory is RED."
    state_key: mic_mute_color
    default: RED
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_mute":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
  custom_led_color:
    type: enum
    values: [LIGHT GREEN, GREEN, BLUE, RED, YELLOW, ORANGE, CYAN, PINK]
    label: Custom LED Colour
    help: "Colour shown while Custom LED Active is on."
    state_key: custom_led_color
    default: BLUE
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
  custom_led_active:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Custom LED Active
    help: "Show the custom colour instead of the mic on/mute colours. Resets to off when the microphone reboots."
    state_key: custom_led_active
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"active":{value}}}}}'
  show_farend_activity:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: Far-End Activity LED
    help: "Let the ring also show audio arriving from the far end."
    state_key: show_farend_activity
    default: "false"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"led":{"show_farend_activity":{value}}}}'

  # ── Network ──
  mdns_enabled:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: mDNS Advertising
    help: "Announce the microphone on the network (Bonjour), which is how Control Cockpit and network scans find it."
    state_key: mdns_enabled
    default: "true"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"device":{"network":{"mdns":{value}}}}'
  dante_interface_mapping:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: AUDIO_SWITCHED, label: Switched (one network on both Dante ports) }
      - { value: AUDIO_REDUNDANT, label: Redundant (primary and secondary networks) }
    label: Dante Port Mode
    help: "The microphone reboots to apply a change."
    state_key: dante_interface_mapping
    default: AUDIO_SWITCHED
    setup: false
    write:
      send: '{"audio":{"out2":{"network":{"ether":{"interface_mapping":"{value}"}}}}}'

# Quick Actions on the device view. The mute pair is gated on the state it
# sets, so only the button that does something shows; the microphone reports
# mute on change, so the button follows the device, not the click.
actions:
  - id: mute_on
    icon: mic-off
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: falsy }
  - id: mute_off
    icon: mic
    visible_when: { key: "device.$id.mute", operator: truthy }
  - id: identify
    icon: sun
  - id: get_beam_position
    icon: crosshair
  - id: restart
    icon: refresh-cw
    confirm: >
      Restart the microphone? Audio drops for about a minute while it boots.

# Every reply and every subscription notification is an SSC address tree, so
# one json rule per feed reads whatever addresses the body carries; a body
# with none of a rule's keys leaves that rule alone. The subscription echo
# ({"osc":{"state":{"subscribe":[...]}}}) carries nulls under "osc" and
# matches nothing here. Array-valued methods are read element by element.
responses:
  # ── Everything that is not a live feed ──
  - json: true
    set:
      product: device.identity.product
      firmware_version: device.identity.version
      serial_number: device.identity.serial
      vendor: device.identity.vendor
      hardware_revision: device.identity.hw_revision
      interface_version: interface.version
      language: device.language
      mac_address: device.network.ether.macs.0
      ip_address: device.network.ipv4.ipaddr.0
      mdns_enabled: device.network.mdns
      device_name: device.name
      location: device.location
      position: device.position
      system_label: device.system
      identify_active: device.identification.visual
      reset_button_pressed: device.button.state
      update_running: device.update.enable
      update_progress: device.update.progress
      update_error: device.update.error
      led_brightness: device.led.brightness
      mic_on_color: device.led.mic_on.color
      mic_mute_color: device.led.mic_mute.color
      custom_led_color: device.led.custom.color
      custom_led_active: device.led.custom.active
      show_farend_activity: device.led.show_farend_activity
      beam_orientation_offset: beam.orientation.offset
      orientation_leds_active: beam.orientation.visual
      mute: audio.mute
      room_in_use: audio.room_in_use
      installation_type: audio.installation_type
      source_detection_threshold: audio.source_detection.threshold
      out1_label: audio.out1.label
      output_attenuation: audio.out1.attenuation
      out2_label: audio.out2.label
      dante_output_gain: audio.out2.gain
      dante_firmware_version: audio.out2.identity.version
      dante_ip_primary: audio.out2.network.ipv4.ipaddr.0
      dante_ip_secondary: audio.out2.network.ipv4.ipaddr.1
      dante_interface_mapping: audio.out2.network.ether.interface_mapping
      ref1_label: audio.ref1.label
      reference_gain: audio.ref1.gain
      farend_auto_adjust: audio.ref1.farend_auto_adjust_enable
      eq_preset: audio.equalizer.preset
      eq_125_hz: audio.equalizer.custom.0
      eq_250_hz: audio.equalizer.custom.1
      eq_500_hz: audio.equalizer.custom.2
      eq_1_khz: audio.equalizer.custom.3
      eq_2_khz: audio.equalizer.custom.4
      eq_4_khz: audio.equalizer.custom.5
      eq_8_khz: audio.equalizer.custom.6
      noise_gate_active: audio.noise_gate.active
      noise_gate_threshold: audio.noise_gate.threshold
      noise_gate_hold_time: audio.noise_gate.hold_time
      voice_lift_active: audio.voice_lift.active
      voice_lift_mute_threshold: audio.voice_lift.emergency_mute_threshold
      voice_lift_mute_time: audio.voice_lift.emergency_mute_time
      priority_zone_active: audio.priority.active.0
      priority_zone_weight: audio.priority.weights.0
      priority_zone_elevation_min: audio.priority.zones.0
      priority_zone_elevation_max: audio.priority.zones.1
      priority_zone_azimuth_min: audio.priority.zones.2
      priority_zone_azimuth_max: audio.priority.zones.3
      exclusion_zone_1_active: audio.exclusion.active.0
      exclusion_zone_2_active: audio.exclusion.active.1
      exclusion_zone_3_active: audio.exclusion.active.2
      exclusion_zone_4_active: audio.exclusion.active.3
      exclusion_zone_5_active: audio.exclusion.active.4
      exclusion_zone_1_elevation_min: audio.exclusion.zones.0.0
      exclusion_zone_1_elevation_max: audio.exclusion.zones.0.1
      exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_min: audio.exclusion.zones.0.2
      exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_max: audio.exclusion.zones.0.3
      exclusion_zone_2_elevation_min: audio.exclusion.zones.1.0
      exclusion_zone_2_elevation_max: audio.exclusion.zones.1.1
      exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_min: audio.exclusion.zones.1.2
      exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_max: audio.exclusion.zones.1.3
      exclusion_zone_3_elevation_min: audio.exclusion.zones.2.0
      exclusion_zone_3_elevation_max: audio.exclusion.zones.2.1
      exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_min: audio.exclusion.zones.2.2
      exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_max: audio.exclusion.zones.2.3
      exclusion_zone_4_elevation_min: audio.exclusion.zones.3.0
      exclusion_zone_4_elevation_max: audio.exclusion.zones.3.1
      exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_min: audio.exclusion.zones.3.2
      exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_max: audio.exclusion.zones.3.3
      exclusion_zone_5_elevation_min: audio.exclusion.zones.4.0
      exclusion_zone_5_elevation_max: audio.exclusion.zones.4.1
      exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_min: audio.exclusion.zones.4.2
      exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_max: audio.exclusion.zones.4.3

  # ── Talker position: a continuous feed while subscribed ──
  # The subscription already asks the microphone for no more than one update
  # per Talker Position Interval; this is the panel-friendly ceiling should
  # the microphone ignore that (drop-style: the next frame carries the
  # current value, so nothing goes stale).
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      beam_azimuth: m.beam.azimuth
      beam_elevation: m.beam.elevation

  # ── Level meters ──
  - json: true
    throttle: 0.2
    set:
      input_peak_db: m.in1.peak
      reference_rms_db: m.ref1.rms

  # ── Errors ── {"osc":{"error":[ {tree:[code,{"desc":"..."}]} ]}} or, for a
  # message the microphone could not parse, {"osc":{"error":[400,{"desc":..}]}}.
  # Nothing above reads a key under "osc", so an error body reaches these.
  # after_json: an SSC reply that answers a good method and a refused one in
  # the same message carries both the value and osc.error. The json rules
  # above resolve the value and would consume the frame, so this rule -- the
  # only one that reads the error -- has to stay eligible past them.
  - match: '"error":\[.*?(\d{3}),\{"desc":"([^"]*)"'
    after_json: true
    set:
      last_error_code: "$1"
      last_error: "$2"

# ── SIMULATOR ──
# One script handler is the whole SSC server: it parses the incoming JSON
# object, walks the address tree against the method table below, answers
# every leaf with its resulting value, records
# subscriptions, bundles the current values into a subscription reply, and
# reports unknown addresses and refused values the way the spec does. Every
# change to a subscribed-style value also goes out as a notification through
# the notifications: map, which is what the real microphone does after it has
# answered a set.
#
# Modelled from the spec, not hardware: out-of-range numbers are adapted to
# the nearest limit and answered without an error (spec §4.2), an enum the
# microphone would refuse answers 406, a read-only address answers its current
# value, and an unknown address answers 404. Array methods honour null for
# "leave this element alone". The 60 s UDP session timeout is not modelled
# (the sandbox has no clock); subscriptions last until cancelled.
simulator:
  initial_state:
    _subscriptions: ""
    product: "TCC2"
    firmware_version: "1.8.0"
    serial_number: "SIM0000001"
    vendor: "Sennheiser electronic GmbH & Co. KG"
    hardware_revision: "1.0"
    interface_version: "1.8.0"
    language: "en_GB"
    mac_address: "00:1B:66:00:00:01"
    ip_address: "192.168.1.60"
    mdns_enabled: true
    device_name: "SLCM2"
    location: "Room"
    position: "over central table"
    system_label: "System"
    mute: false
    room_in_use: false
    identify_active: false
    reset_button_pressed: false
    beam_azimuth: 180
    beam_elevation: 45
    input_peak_db: -60
    reference_rms_db: -80
    out1_label: "Analog Out"
    output_attenuation: 0
    out2_label: "Dante Out"
    dante_output_gain: 12
    dante_firmware_version: "4.2.4.9"
    dante_ip_primary: "169.254.10.10"
    dante_ip_secondary: "172.31.10.10"
    dante_interface_mapping: "AUDIO_SWITCHED"
    ref1_label: "Dante In"
    reference_gain: 0
    farend_auto_adjust: false
    installation_type: "flush_mount"
    source_detection_threshold: "normal_room"
    eq_preset: "OFF"
    eq_125_hz: 0
    eq_250_hz: 0
    eq_500_hz: 0
    eq_1_khz: 0
    eq_2_khz: 0
    eq_4_khz: 0
    eq_8_khz: 0
    noise_gate_active: false
    noise_gate_threshold: -60
    noise_gate_hold_time: 200
    voice_lift_active: false
    voice_lift_mute_threshold: -20
    voice_lift_mute_time: 4
    priority_zone_active: false
    priority_zone_elevation_min: 60
    priority_zone_elevation_max: 80
    priority_zone_azimuth_min: 160
    priority_zone_azimuth_max: 200
    priority_zone_weight: 1.5
    exclusion_zone_1_active: true
    exclusion_zone_1_elevation_min: 0
    exclusion_zone_1_elevation_max: 10
    exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_min: 0
    exclusion_zone_1_azimuth_max: 360
    exclusion_zone_2_active: false
    exclusion_zone_2_elevation_min: 10
    exclusion_zone_2_elevation_max: 50
    exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_min: 20
    exclusion_zone_2_azimuth_max: 70
    exclusion_zone_3_active: false
    exclusion_zone_3_elevation_min: 10
    exclusion_zone_3_elevation_max: 50
    exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_min: 110
    exclusion_zone_3_azimuth_max: 160
    exclusion_zone_4_active: false
    exclusion_zone_4_elevation_min: 10
    exclusion_zone_4_elevation_max: 50
    exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_min: 200
    exclusion_zone_4_azimuth_max: 250
    exclusion_zone_5_active: false
    exclusion_zone_5_elevation_min: 10
    exclusion_zone_5_elevation_max: 50
    exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_min: 290
    exclusion_zone_5_azimuth_max: 340
    beam_orientation_offset: 0
    orientation_leds_active: false
    led_brightness: 5
    mic_on_color: "GREEN"
    mic_mute_color: "RED"
    custom_led_color: "BLUE"
    custom_led_active: false
    show_farend_activity: false
    update_running: false
    update_progress: 0
    update_error: ""
    last_error_code: 0
    last_error: ""

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  controls:
    - type: toggle
      key: mute
      label: Muted
    - type: toggle
      key: room_in_use
      label: Room In Use (talker present)
    - type: slider
      key: beam_azimuth
      label: Talker Azimuth
      min: 0
      max: 359
    - type: slider
      key: beam_elevation
      label: Talker Elevation
      min: 0
      max: 90
    - type: slider
      key: input_peak_db
      label: Input Peak (dB)
      min: -90
      max: 0
    - type: slider
      key: reference_rms_db
      label: AEC Reference (dBFS)
      min: -120
      max: 0
    - type: slider
      key: led_brightness
      label: LED Brightness
      min: 0
      max: 5
    - type: toggle
      key: reset_button_pressed
      label: Reset Button Held
    - type: select
      key: installation_type
      label: Installation Type
      options: ["flush_mount", "suspended"]

  # What the microphone sends, unasked, when a value changes. Booleans need a
  # template per value (the JSON literal), strings are quoted, numbers bare.
  # Array-valued methods (equalizer bands, zones) have no per-element frame;
  # the reply to a set carries the whole array instead.
  notifications:
    mute:
      'true': '{"audio":{"mute":true}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"mute":false}}'
    room_in_use:
      'true': '{"audio":{"room_in_use":true}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"room_in_use":false}}'
    identify_active:
      'true': '{"device":{"identification":{"visual":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"identification":{"visual":false}}}'
    reset_button_pressed:
      'true': '{"device":{"button":{"state":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"button":{"state":false}}}'
    beam_azimuth: '{"m":{"beam":{"azimuth":{value}}}}'
    beam_elevation: '{"m":{"beam":{"elevation":{value}}}}'
    input_peak_db: '{"m":{"in1":{"peak":{value}}}}'
    reference_rms_db: '{"m":{"ref1":{"rms":{value}}}}'
    output_attenuation: '{"audio":{"out1":{"attenuation":{value}}}}'
    dante_output_gain: '{"audio":{"out2":{"gain":{value}}}}'
    reference_gain: '{"audio":{"ref1":{"gain":{value}}}}'
    farend_auto_adjust:
      'true': '{"audio":{"ref1":{"farend_auto_adjust_enable":true}}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"ref1":{"farend_auto_adjust_enable":false}}}'
    installation_type: '{"audio":{"installation_type":"{value}"}}'
    source_detection_threshold: '{"audio":{"source_detection":{"threshold":"{value}"}}}'
    eq_preset: '{"audio":{"equalizer":{"preset":"{value}"}}}'
    noise_gate_active:
      'true': '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"active":true}}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"active":false}}}'
    noise_gate_threshold: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"threshold":{value}}}}'
    noise_gate_hold_time: '{"audio":{"noise_gate":{"hold_time":{value}}}}'
    voice_lift_active:
      'true': '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"active":true}}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"active":false}}}'
    voice_lift_mute_threshold: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"emergency_mute_threshold":{value}}}}'
    voice_lift_mute_time: '{"audio":{"voice_lift":{"emergency_mute_time":{value}}}}'
    priority_zone_active:
      'true': '{"audio":{"priority":{"active":[true]}}}'
      'false': '{"audio":{"priority":{"active":[false]}}}'
    priority_zone_weight: '{"audio":{"priority":{"weights":[{value}]}}}'
    beam_orientation_offset: '{"beam":{"orientation":{"offset":{value}}}}'
    orientation_leds_active:
      'true': '{"beam":{"orientation":{"visual":true}}}'
      'false': '{"beam":{"orientation":{"visual":false}}}'
    led_brightness: '{"device":{"led":{"brightness":{value}}}}'
    mic_on_color: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_on":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
    mic_mute_color: '{"device":{"led":{"mic_mute":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
    custom_led_color: '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"color":"{value}"}}}}'
    custom_led_active:
      'true': '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"active":true}}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"led":{"custom":{"active":false}}}}'
    show_farend_activity:
      'true': '{"device":{"led":{"show_farend_activity":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"led":{"show_farend_activity":false}}}'
    mdns_enabled:
      'true': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"network":{"mdns":false}}}'
    device_name: '{"device":{"name":"{value}"}}'
    location: '{"device":{"location":"{value}"}}'
    position: '{"device":{"position":"{value}"}}'
    system_label: '{"device":{"system":"{value}"}}'
    dante_interface_mapping: '{"audio":{"out2":{"network":{"ether":{"interface_mapping":"{value}"}}}}}'
    update_running:
      'true': '{"device":{"update":{"enable":true}}}'
      'false': '{"device":{"update":{"enable":false}}}'
    update_progress: '{"device":{"update":{"progress":{value}}}}'
    update_error: '{"device":{"update":{"error":"{value}"}}}'

  command_handlers:
    # Everything the socket receives goes through the one SSC server, so a
    # truncated or non-JSON datagram gets the spec's 400, not silence.
    - match: '(?s:.*)'
      handler: |
        def _run():
            text = match.group(0)

            # ── JSON on the wire ──
            # json.loads / json.dumps are available to a script handler from
            # platform 0.34.0, which this driver requires; before that a JSON
            # simulator had to bring its own reader and writer.
            #
            # The writer keeps one rule the stdlib does not have: a whole
            # float prints as an integer. SSC integer methods pass through
            # float arithmetic on the way here (clamping, averaging), and the
            # microphone answers 5, never 5.0.
            def plain(v):
                cls = v.__class__
                if cls is float and v == int(v):
                    return int(v)
                if cls is dict:
                    return {k: plain(x) for k, x in v.items()}
                if cls is list or cls is tuple:
                    return [plain(x) for x in v]
                return v

            def dumps(v):
                return json.dumps(
                    plain(v), separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False
                )

            # ── The method table: dotted address -> (kind, state key, limits) ──
            # kinds: bool / num / int / str / enum (options) / const (read-only)
            # arr: a list of element specs, or a list of lists for nested arrays
            COLORS = ["LIGHT GREEN", "GREEN", "BLUE", "RED", "YELLOW", "ORANGE", "CYAN", "PINK"]
            def zone(i):
                return [
                    ("int", "exclusion_zone_%d_elevation_min" % i, 0, 90),
                    ("int", "exclusion_zone_%d_elevation_max" % i, 0, 90),
                    ("int", "exclusion_zone_%d_azimuth_min" % i, 0, 360),
                    ("int", "exclusion_zone_%d_azimuth_max" % i, 0, 360),
                ]
            LEAVES = {
                "device.identity.product": ("const", "product"),
                "device.identity.version": ("const", "firmware_version"),
                "device.identity.serial": ("const", "serial_number"),
                "device.identity.vendor": ("const", "vendor"),
                "device.identity.hw_revision": ("const", "hardware_revision"),
                "device.language": ("const", "language"),
                "device.network.ether.macs": ("arr", [("const", "mac_address")]),
                "device.network.ipv4.ipaddr": ("arr", [("const", "ip_address")]),
                "device.network.mdns": ("bool", "mdns_enabled"),
                "device.name": ("str", "device_name", 8),
                "device.location": ("str", "location", 100),
                "device.position": ("str", "position", 30),
                "device.system": ("str", "system_label", 30),
                "device.identification.visual": ("bool", "identify_active"),
                "device.button.state": ("const", "reset_button_pressed"),
                "device.update.enable": ("bool", "update_running"),
                "device.update.progress": ("const", "update_progress"),
                "device.update.error": ("const", "update_error"),
                "device.led.brightness": ("int", "led_brightness", 0, 5),
                "device.led.mic_on.color": ("enum", "mic_on_color", COLORS),
                "device.led.mic_mute.color": ("enum", "mic_mute_color", COLORS),
                "device.led.custom.color": ("enum", "custom_led_color", COLORS),
                "device.led.custom.active": ("bool", "custom_led_active"),
                "device.led.show_farend_activity": ("bool", "show_farend_activity"),
                "device.restart": ("trigger", None),
                "device.restore": ("enum", None, ["FACTORY_DEFAULTS", "AUDIO_DEFAULTS", "DANTE_FACTORY_DEFAULTS"]),
                "interface.version": ("const", "interface_version"),
                "audio.mute": ("bool", "mute"),
                "audio.room_in_use": ("const", "room_in_use"),
                "audio.installation_type": ("enum", "installation_type", ["flush_mount", "suspended"]),
                "audio.source_detection.threshold": ("enum", "source_detection_threshold", ["quiet_room", "normal_room", "loud_room"]),
                "audio.out1.label": ("const", "out1_label"),
                "audio.out1.attenuation": ("num", "output_attenuation", -18, 0),
                "audio.out2.label": ("const", "out2_label"),
                "audio.out2.gain": ("num", "dante_output_gain", 0, 24),
                "audio.out2.identity.version": ("const", "dante_firmware_version"),
                "audio.out2.network.ipv4.ipaddr": ("arr", [("const", "dante_ip_primary"), ("const", "dante_ip_secondary")]),
                "audio.out2.network.ether.interface_mapping": ("enum", "dante_interface_mapping", ["AUDIO_SWITCHED", "AUDIO_REDUNDANT"]),
                "audio.ref1.label": ("const", "ref1_label"),
                "audio.ref1.gain": ("num", "reference_gain", -60, 10),
                "audio.ref1.farend_auto_adjust_enable": ("bool", "farend_auto_adjust"),
                "audio.equalizer.preset": ("enum", "eq_preset", ["OFF", "CUSTOM"]),
                "audio.equalizer.custom": ("arr", [
                    ("num", "eq_125_hz", -8, 8), ("num", "eq_250_hz", -8, 8),
                    ("num", "eq_500_hz", -8, 8), ("num", "eq_1_khz", -8, 8),
                    ("num", "eq_2_khz", -8, 8), ("num", "eq_4_khz", -8, 8),
                    ("num", "eq_8_khz", -8, 8)]),
                "audio.noise_gate.active": ("bool", "noise_gate_active"),
                "audio.noise_gate.threshold": ("num", "noise_gate_threshold", -90, -40),
                "audio.noise_gate.hold_time": ("int", "noise_gate_hold_time", 50, 1000),
                "audio.voice_lift.active": ("bool", "voice_lift_active"),
                "audio.voice_lift.emergency_mute_threshold": ("num", "voice_lift_mute_threshold", -50, -3),
                "audio.voice_lift.emergency_mute_time": ("num", "voice_lift_mute_time", 1, 30),
                "audio.priority.active": ("arr", [("bool", "priority_zone_active")]),
                "audio.priority.weights": ("arr", [("num", "priority_zone_weight", 1, 4)]),
                "audio.priority.zones": ("arr", [
                    ("int", "priority_zone_elevation_min", 0, 90),
                    ("int", "priority_zone_elevation_max", 0, 90),
                    ("int", "priority_zone_azimuth_min", 0, 360),
                    ("int", "priority_zone_azimuth_max", 0, 360)]),
                "audio.exclusion.active": ("arr", [
                    ("bool", "exclusion_zone_1_active"), ("bool", "exclusion_zone_2_active"),
                    ("bool", "exclusion_zone_3_active"), ("bool", "exclusion_zone_4_active"),
                    ("bool", "exclusion_zone_5_active")]),
                "audio.exclusion.zones": ("arr", [
                    ("arr", zone(1)), ("arr", zone(2)), ("arr", zone(3)),
                    ("arr", zone(4)), ("arr", zone(5))]),
                "beam.orientation.offset": ("enum", "beam_orientation_offset", [0, 90, 180, 270]),
                "beam.orientation.visual": ("bool", "orientation_leds_active"),
                "m.beam.azimuth": ("const", "beam_azimuth"),
                "m.beam.elevation": ("const", "beam_elevation"),
                "m.in1.peak": ("const", "input_peak_db"),
                "m.ref1.rms": ("const", "reference_rms_db"),
            }
            SUBSCRIBABLE = [p for p in LEAVES if not p.startswith("device.identity") and p not in ("device.language", "interface.version", "device.restart", "device.restore", "audio.out1.label", "audio.out2.label", "audio.ref1.label", "audio.out2.identity.version", "device.network.ether.macs")]

            reply = {}
            errors = []

            def put(tree, path, value):
                node = tree
                for seg in path[:-1]:
                    if seg not in node or node[seg].__class__ is not dict:
                        node[seg] = {}
                    node = node[seg]
                node[path[-1]] = value

            def fail(path, code, desc):
                tree = {}
                put(tree, path, [code, {"desc": desc}])
                errors.append(tree)

            def current(spec):
                kind = spec[0]
                if kind == "arr":
                    return [current(el) for el in spec[1]]
                if kind == "trigger":
                    return None
                if spec[1] is None:
                    return None
                return state[spec[1]]

            # A refused method is reported under osc.error and left out of the
            # value tree, as in the spec's own example (§5.1.2); OMIT marks it.
            OMIT = ("omit",)

            def apply(spec, value, path):
                # Returns the resulting value (the reply), recording errors.
                kind = spec[0]
                if kind == "arr":
                    elems = spec[1]
                    if value.__class__ is not list:
                        value = [value]
                    if len(value) > len(elems):
                        fail(path, 416, "requested range not satisfiable")
                        return OMIT
                    out = []
                    for i, el in enumerate(elems):
                        v = value[i] if i < len(value) else None
                        res = current(el) if v is None else apply(el, v, path)
                        out.append(current(el) if res is OMIT else res)
                    return out
                if kind == "const":
                    return state[spec[1]]
                if kind == "trigger":
                    return value
                if kind == "bool":
                    state[spec[1]] = bool(value)
                    return state[spec[1]]
                if kind == "str":
                    s = str(value)[: spec[2]]
                    state[spec[1]] = s
                    return s
                if kind == "enum":
                    if value not in spec[2]:
                        fail(path, 406, "not acceptable")
                        return OMIT
                    if spec[1] is not None:
                        state[spec[1]] = value
                    return value
                # num / int: out-of-range values are adapted, not refused
                try:
                    num = float(value)
                except (TypeError, ValueError):
                    fail(path, 406, "not acceptable")
                    return OMIT
                num = max(spec[2], min(spec[3], num))
                if kind == "int" or num == int(num):
                    num = int(num)
                state[spec[1]] = num
                return num

            def subscribed():
                s = state["_subscriptions"]
                return [p for p in s.split(",") if p]

            def leaves_of(tree, prefix):
                # Every (path, value) pair below a request node, as dotted paths.
                out = []
                for key, val in tree.items():
                    if key == "#":
                        continue
                    path = prefix + [key]
                    if val.__class__ is dict:
                        dotted = ".".join(path)
                        if dotted in LEAVES:
                            out.append((path, val))
                        else:
                            out.extend(leaves_of(val, path))
                    else:
                        out.append((path, val))
                return out

            def handle_subscribe(value):
                if value is None:
                    tree = {}
                    for p in subscribed():
                        put(tree, p.split("."), None)
                    put(reply, ["osc", "state", "subscribe"], [tree])
                    return
                if value.__class__ is not list:
                    value = [value]
                subs = subscribed()
                for entry in value:
                    if entry.__class__ is not dict:
                        continue
                    params = entry.get("#") or {}
                    cancel = bool(params.get("cancel", False))
                    for path, _val in leaves_of(entry, []):
                        dotted = ".".join(path)
                        if dotted not in SUBSCRIBABLE:
                            fail(["osc", "state", "subscribe"] + path, 454, "parameter address not found")
                            continue
                        if cancel:
                            subs = [p for p in subs if p != dotted]
                        else:
                            if dotted not in subs:
                                subs.append(dotted)
                            # Initial notification, bundled with the reply.
                            put(reply, path, current(LEAVES[dotted]))
                state["_subscriptions"] = ",".join(subs)
                put(reply, ["osc", "state", "subscribe"], value)

            def handle(path, value):
                dotted = ".".join(path)
                if dotted == "osc.ping" or dotted == "osc.xid":
                    put(reply, path, value)
                elif dotted == "osc.version":
                    put(reply, path, "1.2")
                elif dotted == "osc.error":
                    pass  # answered below, from what this message produced
                elif dotted == "osc.state.subscribe":
                    handle_subscribe(value)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.close":
                    state["_subscriptions"] = ""
                    put(reply, path, True)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.prettyprint":
                    put(reply, path, False)
                elif dotted == "osc.state.auth.access":
                    put(reply, path, "default:/")
                elif dotted == "osc.feature.subscription":
                    put(reply, path, True)
                elif dotted == "osc.feature.pattern":
                    put(reply, path, "*?")
                elif dotted in ("osc.feature.timetag", "osc.feature.baseaddr"):
                    put(reply, path, False)
                elif dotted in LEAVES:
                    spec = LEAVES[dotted]
                    if value is None:
                        put(reply, path, current(spec))
                    else:
                        result = apply(spec, value, path)
                        if result is not OMIT:
                            put(reply, path, result)
                else:
                    fail(path, 404, "address not found")

            try:
                request = json.loads(text)
                if request.__class__ is not dict:
                    raise ValueError("not an object")
            except ValueError:
                respond('{"osc":{"error":[400,{"desc":"not understood"}]}}')
                return

            for path, value in leaves_of(request, []):
                handle(path, value)
            if errors:
                put(reply, ["osc", "error"], errors)
            elif "osc" in request and request["osc"].__class__ is dict and "error" in request["osc"]:
                put(reply, ["osc", "error"], [])
            respond(dumps(reply))

        _run()
